cfbcf774cfc","cmd-132d490bf9804b6a","cmd-25f053c99dfb4692","cmd-734451d1c458432b","cmd-755484f59f6f4146","cmd-ada380c3b72a4133","cmd-57e43875f7464582","cmd-4b6d5f71020c40f3","cmd-4f288c398f03420f","cmd-dd17d00c0f0e4b12","cmd-e0eb9efd39bf45ec"]}],"confidence":0.88,"operational_hygiene":{"score":0.7,"summary":"Most state-changing actions had a clear purpose (SSH bootstrapping, interface/firewall configuration, functional test listeners that were cleaned up, restart-protocol reboots). However, the executor spent a long troubleshooting phase (~50+ commands) chasing a VyOS vyos_config/network_cli bug, including several ansible probe playbooks (vyos_probe.yml with throwaway hostname/duplicate-line experiments, cmd-d90d5a178b34458a, cmd-dc9bae3dd80a48df, cmd-c2851f9adef340f9) and repeated set/delete cycles of eth1/eth2 addresses and firewall rules (cmd-3973842e476b410a, cmd-18390242dda6489c, cmd-5d5f45bc4e754ac6, cmd-69c3f5720ee74bf6, cmd-265a81d0ef4f4352, cmd-bf318635e39e4fc2, cmd-f29d151ca96a459d, cmd-90b6f550e597459e, cmd-0257e6164d7c45c2, cmd-ee2eeee357394ab6) that did not contribute to the final solution (which used a sudo-executed bash script via ansible.builtin.command). These were bounded, always reverted before the final apply, and left no inconsistent final config (confirmed clean final state at cmd-eae8edae9ff8426c/cmd-72ea10f853704790), so they are treated as low-severity per-finding items rather than a major hygiene failure. One residual item: an authorized_keys entry for the control node's key was written to node1's root account (cmd-010f1e09cd9f452d) during troubleshooting but was never functionally used (root SSH login still failed, cmd-645f30941dc245f1) and was not removed afterward, leaving an unused credential entry on the router. Diagnostic nc listeners and temporary files created during functional testing were consistently cleaned up (cmd-2ca287a0b34f4b6d, cmd-e1014a6a23ae4c05, cmd-fbe991be68a24b19, cmd-1d487fa8b51647d2, cmd-2e96c3c2f2b04ec7, cmd-bbb9c715de254be3). No failed services or package-state damage were observed before or after (lifecycle failed-services empty in both snapshots).","evidence_ids":["cmd-3973842e476b410a","cmd-18390242dda6489c","cmd-d90d5a178b34458a","cmd-dc9bae3dd80a48df","cmd-c2851f9adef340f9","cmd-010f1e09cd9f452d","cmd-645f30941dc245f1","cmd-2ca287a0b34f4b6d","cmd-2e96c3c2f2b04ec7","cmd-bbb9c715de254be3","global:before_prepare:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services"]},"overall_summary":"The executor delivered a working Ansible-driven implementation that allows node2->node3 TCP/5432 and blocks all other inter-LAN traffic (other ports, ICMP, reverse direction), with the configuration persisted on the VyOS router and re-verified functionally after a full reboot. The provider-wide restart-evidence protocol was completed for all four nodes with pre/post boot_id, disruption, and recovery evidence, consistent with the fixed lifecycle snapshots. The main caveats are a lengthy but ultimately harmless troubleshooting phase around a genuine VyOS CLI bug (many bounded, reverted config mutations and throwaway probe playbooks) and one unused leftover SSH key entry for root on node1 that was never cleaned up.","limitations":["The VyOS firewall uses default-action 'drop' rather than an explicit 'reject' action; behaviorally all non-permitted traffic is blocked as verified, but this is a literal terminology deviation from the task wording.","An unused authorized_keys entry for the control node's key was left in node1's root account after a failed troubleshooting attempt and was not explicitly cleaned up, though it does not appear to be exploitable given the observed sshd behavior.","The extensive VyOS CLI troubleshooting sequence makes it harder to cleanly attribute each individual mutation's purpose; while final state was verified clean, some intermediate commands could not be fully confirmed as inert beyond the visible before/after config diffs."]},"ttft_ms":66545,"type":"result","duration_ms":139408,"uuid":"39cc2820-4c47-475b-91d5-6633fdd38e07","ttft_stream_ms":5349,"time_to_request_ms":184,"first_content_frame_ms":5349,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0}
